\paragraph{Single-LLM confound.}
Both training and synthetic OOD data are generated by Qwen3-8B, raising the concern that the evidence hierarchy reflects within-LLM stylistic transfer rather than discourse-level generalization. Evaluation on two independent human datasets, ToxicChat~\citep{lin2023toxicchat} (204 LMSYS jailbreaks) and a community corpus (666 Reddit/Discord jailbreaks), provides partial resolution: all domain-adapted variants outperform vanilla by 3--7$\times$ across both datasets (Table~\ref{tab:human_data}), confirming that DAPT on synthetic text transfers to human-written attacks regardless of source population. Both datasets are single-turn, so the relative ordering among domain-adapted variants reflects single-turn modality rather than variant quality. This evidence validates the core DAPT benefit but does not test the full multi-turn pipeline; multi-turn human jailbreak datasets are needed to confirm the complete hierarchy.

\paragraph{Encoder capacity confound.}
